# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  AI Research Assistant — Environment Variables
#  Copy this file to .env and fill in ONE provider below.
#  DO NOT commit .env to version control.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── OPTION 1: Google Gemini (RECOMMENDED FREE option) ──────────────
# Preferred automatically when both Gemini and Groq keys are configured.
# Sign up FREE at: https://aistudio.google.com
# Click "Get API Key" → copy and paste below
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIzaxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── OPTION 2: Groq (FREE; subject to model-specific rate limits) ────
# Sign up FREE at: https://console.groq.com
# Click "API Keys" → "Create API Key" → copy and paste below
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── OPTION 3: Ollama (100% LOCAL — no internet, no account needed) ──
# Install from: https://ollama.ai  then run: ollama pull llama3.2
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# ── OPTION 4: Anthropic Claude (PAID — $5 free credits for new users)
# Sign up at: https://console.anthropic.com
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ── Optional: override the default model for your chosen provider ────
# Set a Groq model explicitly here to continue using Groq when both keys exist.
# LLM_MODEL=groq/qwen/qwen3.8-27b
# LLM_MODEL=gemini/gemini-3.8-flash
